cartridge "GREAT CANADIAN MYSTERY/AMY STUDIO/2026"

' THE GREAT CANADIAN MYSTERY SHOW - version 2 (original game).
' Design: Amy (Amy Studio). Program, pictures, effects, jingles: Claude
' (Anthropic), in the Amy language. Title theme: Amy's sting. People
' portraits and presenter: the redrawn set Amy approved (gcm-art).
'
' 32 cases made offline by gen.py (11 destinations, 6 fictional persons
' with 3 traits each, 4 incident types). Each case: a 3-leg route, 3 choices
' per stop (the lead rules out the 2 others), 2 ID clues that single out one
' person, a deadline that the shortest winning plan fills to 60-75 %.
' A new episode picks a case (never the last one); RETRY CASE replays it.
'
' Clock (NORMAL): a witness with a hint (lead or ID clue) +2h, without
' +1h (first time only), right trip +3h, wrong trip +4h (round trip, clues
' kept), alert +2h; atlas, dossier, menus free. HARD (title LEVEL item,
' kept by RETRY CASE, "HARD" in the HUD): every witness +2h, wrong +5h.
' Same cases and deadlines on both levels.
' Endings: solved (score 1000 + 25 x hours left); deadline; wrong person;
' no alert and no time to file one; END CASE (the player quits). Each
' ending shows its reason; one press returns to the title. Ending text
' stays in columns 4-20: columns 21-28, rows 3-10 are kept for ending art.
'
' Controls: either controller. Stick up/down moves, button 1 = OK, button
' 2 = back. No keypad needed. Atlas, dossier and END CASE are menu items.
'
' Screen: `bitmap screen`. Codes 0-149: the font in three colours in every
' third; 150-255: the current picture (art.py, ZX0). Text: pages of words
' from one dictionary (gen.py), drawn by DrawText. Text box and HUD lines
' are double-spaced (rows 13/15/17 and 19/21). Everything readable is in
' columns 2-29, rows 1-22.
' Sound: music first (title sting, YOU WIN, YOU LOSE: 4 voices each in
' $702B..$7049), effects after ($7053 tone 1, $705D noise), louder.
' House rules: NewScreen/ShowScreen with the NMI and display off, frame
' loop Rearm/wait/nmi off, no `call asm`, the title loops from the top.

